/-!
# Native interpretation of the Held elementary commutation graph

The vertices are original Sylow words. Existing word coverage gives all
square-one elements. Four faithful base points check every advertised product
and reject noncommuting pairs. All finite computations run in the kernel.
Source: the original ATLAS Held carrier and Aschbacher--Smith 12.7.5, p.840.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace Held.OrdinaryElementary.NativeCoverage
